# Version control and local working directories. Nothing here reaches an image
# today only because worker.Dockerfile and datasets.Dockerfile COPY named paths
# rather than `COPY . .`; local working files can hold credentials, so that
# selective COPY is load-bearing. Excluding them here makes it a property of the
# build context instead of a property of each Dockerfile.
# .git is safe to drop: the version is a static literal in pyproject.toml, there is
# no setuptools-scm, and worker.Dockerfile's `git` is apt-get installing the binary.
.git/
.dev/
.claude/
